[meta]
lang: en
title: OireMark conformance tests: Lists
[/meta]

h1. Lists

Tests for Section 9 of the specification.

h2. Space after the marker

h3. Bold text at line start is not a list {#lists-no-space-bold}
[code om]
*bold* word
[/code]
[code html]
<p><strong>bold</strong> word</p>
[/code]

h3. Hashtag at line start is not a list {#lists-no-space-hashtag}
[code om]
#hashtag
[/code]
[code html]
<p>#hashtag</p>
[/code]

h3. Deleted text at line start is not a list {#lists-no-space-deleted}
[code om]
-deleted- text
[/code]
[code html]
<p><del>deleted</del> text</p>
[/code]

h3. Number without a space is not a list {#lists-no-space-number}
[code om]
1.Item
[/code]
[code html]
<p>1.Item</p>
[/code]

h3. A decimal number is not a list {#lists-decimal}
[code om]
1.1 is a decimal
[/code]
[code html]
<p>1.1 is a decimal</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped marker is text {#lists-escaped-marker}
[code om]
\* Not an item
[/code]
[code html]
<p>* Not an item</p>
[/code]

h3. Escaped number is text {#lists-escaped-number}
[code om]
1984\. A good year.
[/code]
[code html]
<p>1984. A good year.</p>
[/code]

h3. A lone marker is a paragraph {#lists-lone-marker}
[code om]
*
[/code]
[code html]
<p>*</p>
[/code]

h3. A lone marker after an item continues it {#lists-lone-marker-continuation}
[code om]
* Item
*
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item<br>
  *</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. A list item ends a paragraph without a blank line {#lists-interrupt-paragraph}
[code om]
Shopping list:
* Milk
* Eggs
[/code]
[code html]
<p>Shopping list:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Milk</li>
  <li>Eggs</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Whitespace inside an item is kept {#lists-inner-whitespace}
[code om]
* two  spaces
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>two  spaces</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Indentation is ignored {#lists-indented}
[code om]
    * Indented item
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Indented item</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h2. Bulleted lists

h3. Asterisk bullets {#lists-bullet-asterisk}
[code om]
* Item one
* Item two
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item one</li>
  <li>Item two</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Hyphen bullets {#lists-bullet-hyphen}
[code om]
- Item one
- Item two
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item one</li>
  <li>Item two</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Asterisks and hyphens mix at the top level {#lists-bullet-mixed}
[code om]
* Item one
- Item two
* Item three
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item one</li>
  <li>Item two</li>
  <li>Item three</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Double hyphen is not a list marker {#lists-double-hyphen-paragraph}
[code om]
-- not a list
[/code]
[code html]
<p>-- not a list</p>
[/code]

h3. Double hyphen after an item continues it {#lists-double-hyphen-continuation}
[code om]
- Item
-- more text
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item<br>
  -- more text</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Hyphen in an ancestry path is not a list marker {#lists-hash-hyphen-paragraph}
[code om]
#- not a list
[/code]
[code html]
<p>#- not a list</p>
[/code]

h3. Inline formatting in items {#lists-item-formatting}
[code om]
* This is *bold* and _italic_
* Item with `code` and [a link]:https://example.com
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>This is <strong>bold</strong> and <em>italic</em></li>
  <li>Item with <code>code</code> and <a href="https://example.com">a link</a></li>
</ul>
[/code]

h2. Numbered lists

h3. Hash markers {#lists-numbered-hash}
[code om]
# Item one
# Item two
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Item one</li>
  <li>Item two</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Explicit numbers starting at 1 {#lists-numbered-explicit}
[code om]
1. Item one
2. Item two
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Item one</li>
  <li>Item two</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. First number sets the start {#lists-start-number}
[code om]
5. Fifth step
6. Sixth step
[/code]
[code html]
<ol start="5">
  <li>Fifth step</li>
  <li>Sixth step</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Zero is a valid start {#lists-start-zero}
[code om]
0. Zero
1. One
[/code]
[code html]
<ol start="0">
  <li>Zero</li>
  <li>One</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Leading zeros carry no meaning {#lists-start-leading-zeros}
[code om]
05. Five
06. Six
[/code]
[code html]
<ol start="5">
  <li>Five</li>
  <li>Six</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Leading zeros on a following item {#lists-leading-zeros-in-sequence}
[code om]
1. One
02. Two
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>One</li>
  <li>Two</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Hash after a start number continues the count {#lists-start-then-hash}
[code om]
5. Fifth step
# Sixth step
7. Seventh step
[/code]
[code html]
<ol start="5">
  <li>Fifth step</li>
  <li>Sixth step</li>
  <li>Seventh step</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h2. Mixing hash and explicit numbers

h3. Explicit number that follows on {#lists-mix-in-sequence}
[code om]
1. Apples
# Pears
# Plums
4. Oranges
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Apples</li>
  <li>Pears</li>
  <li>Plums</li>
  <li>Oranges</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Explicit number that jumps ahead {#lists-mix-jump}
[code om]
1. Apples
# Pears
7. Plums
# Oranges
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Apples</li>
  <li>Pears</li>
  <li value="7">Plums</li>
  <li>Oranges</li>
</ol>
[/code]
[code warnings]
list-number-jump 3
[/code]

h3. Explicit number that goes back {#lists-mix-backward}
[code om]
1. One
2. Two
2. Two again
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>One</li>
  <li>Two</li>
  <li value="2">Two again</li>
</ol>
[/code]
[code warnings]
list-number-jump 3
[/code]

h3. Hash list followed by a mismatched number {#lists-mix-hash-first}
[code om]
# One
5. Five
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>One</li>
  <li value="5">Five</li>
</ol>
[/code]
[code warnings]
list-number-jump 2
[/code]

h2. Continuation lines

h3. Unmarked lines continue the item {#lists-continuation}
[code om]
* Oire Software
12 Main Street
Springfield
* Another item
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Oire Software<br>
  12 Main Street<br>
  Springfield</li>
  <li>Another item</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Continuation with formatting at line start {#lists-continuation-formatting}
[code om]
* Item
*bold* text
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item<br>
  <strong>bold</strong> text</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Escaped marker continues the item {#lists-continuation-escaped}
[code om]
* Item
\* not a new item
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item<br>
  * not a new item</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Continuation of a nested item {#lists-continuation-nested}
[code om]
* Outer
** Inner
more inner text
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Outer
    <ul>
      <li>Inner<br>
      more inner text</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Heading ends the list {#lists-ended-by-heading}
[code om]
* Item
h2. Heading
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="heading">Heading</h2>
[/code]

h3. Short form quote ends the list {#lists-ended-by-quote}
[code om]
* Item
> Quoted
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item</li>
</ul>
<blockquote>
  <p>Quoted</p>
</blockquote>
[/code]

h3. Horizontal rule ends the list {#lists-ended-by-rule}
[code om]
* Item
---
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item</li>
</ul>
<hr>
[/code]

h3. Table row ends the list {#lists-ended-by-table}
[code om]
* Item
| a | b |
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item</li>
</ul>
<table>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>a</td><td>b</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
[/code]

h3. Definition marker ends the list {#lists-ended-by-definition}
[code om]
* Item
; Term
: Definition
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item</li>
</ul>
<dl>
  <dt>Term</dt>
  <dd>Definition</dd>
</dl>
[/code]

h3. Block tag ends the list {#lists-ended-by-block-tag}
[code om]
* Item
[note]
Note text.
[/note]
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item</li>
</ul>
<div role="note" class="note">
  <p>Note text.</p>
</div>
[/code]

h3. Code fence ends the list {#lists-ended-by-fence}
[code om]
* Item
```
code
```
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item</li>
</ul>
<pre><code>code
</code></pre>
[/code]

h2. Nesting

h3. Nested bullets {#lists-nested-bullets}
[code om]
* Level 1
** Level 2
*** Level 3
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Level 1
    <ul>
      <li>Level 2
        <ul>
          <li>Level 3</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Nested hash numbers {#lists-nested-hash}
[code om]
# Level 1
## Level 2
# Back to level 1
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Level 1
    <ol>
      <li>Level 2</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li>Back to level 1</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Returning to the outer level {#lists-nested-return}
[code om]
* a
** b
* c
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>a
    <ul>
      <li>b</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>c</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Nested explicit numbers {#lists-nested-explicit}
[code om]
1. First
1.1. Nested
1.2. Another nested
2. Second
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>First
    <ol>
      <li>Nested</li>
      <li>Another nested</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li>Second</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Last component of a nested number sets its start {#lists-nested-start}
[code om]
1. First
1.3. Nested
2. Second
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>First
    <ol start="3">
      <li>Nested</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
  <li>Second</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Jump inside a nested list {#lists-nested-jump}
[code om]
1. First
1.1. a
1.3. b
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>First
    <ol>
      <li>a</li>
      <li value="3">b</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ol>
[/code]
[code warnings]
list-number-jump 3
[/code]

h3. Mismatched prefix still nests by depth {#lists-nested-prefix-mismatch}
The prefix warning is only SHOULD, so it is not asserted.
[code om]
1. First
2.1. Nested
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>First
    <ol>
      <li>Nested</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Mixed types by ancestry path {#lists-nested-mixed}
[code om]
# Shopping
#* Milk
#* Eggs
#* Bread
# Chores
#* Call mom
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Shopping
    <ul>
      <li>Milk</li>
      <li>Eggs</li>
      <li>Bread</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>Chores
    <ul>
      <li>Call mom</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Three levels of mixed types {#lists-nested-mixed-deep}
[code om]
# Numbered
#* Bullet
#*# Deep
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Numbered
    <ul>
      <li>Bullet
        <ol>
          <li>Deep</li>
        </ol>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Numbered inside bullet {#lists-nested-numbered-in-bullet}
[code om]
* Bullet item
*# Numbered inside bullet
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Bullet item
    <ol>
      <li>Numbered inside bullet</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Skipped level is an error {#lists-nested-skipped-level}
[code om]
* Level 1
*** Level 3
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 2
[/code]

h3. Skipped explicit number level is an error {#lists-nested-skipped-explicit}
[code om]
1. First
1.1.1. Too deep
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 2
[/code]

h3. Nested marker with no parent is an error {#lists-nested-orphan}
[code om]
** Orphan
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 1
[/code]

h3. Mixed nested marker with no parent is an error {#lists-nested-orphan-mixed}
[code om]
#* Orphan
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 1
[/code]

h3. Nested marker after a paragraph has no parent {#lists-nested-orphan-after-paragraph}
[code om]
Text
** Orphan
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 2
[/code]

h3. Ancestry path that does not match is an error {#lists-nested-path-mismatch}
[code om]
# a
*# b
[/code]
[code error]
invalid-nesting 2
[/code]

h2. Changing type at the top level

h3. Bullet after a hash list starts a new list {#lists-type-change-hash-bullet}
[code om]
# Numbered
* Bulleted
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Numbered</li>
</ol>
<ul>
  <li>Bulleted</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Bullet after an explicit number starts a new list {#lists-type-change-number-bullet}
[code om]
1. Numbered
* Bulleted
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Numbered</li>
</ol>
<ul>
  <li>Bulleted</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Hash after a bullet list starts a new list {#lists-type-change-bullet-hash}
[code om]
* Bulleted
# Numbered
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Bulleted</li>
</ul>
<ol>
  <li>Numbered</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h2. Style hints

h3. Uppercase letters {#lists-hint-upper-alpha}
[code om]
#(A) First item
# Second item
# Third item
[/code]
[code html]
<ol type="A">
  <li>First item</li>
  <li>Second item</li>
  <li>Third item</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Lowercase letters {#lists-hint-lower-alpha}
[code om]
#(a) First item
# Second item
[/code]
[code html]
<ol type="a">
  <li>First item</li>
  <li>Second item</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Uppercase Roman numerals {#lists-hint-upper-roman}
[code om]
#(I) First item
# Second item
[/code]
[code html]
<ol type="I">
  <li>First item</li>
  <li>Second item</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Lowercase Roman numerals {#lists-hint-lower-roman}
[code om]
#(i) First item
# Second item
[/code]
[code html]
<ol type="i">
  <li>First item</li>
  <li>Second item</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. The default hint adds no type {#lists-hint-default}
[code om]
#(1) First item
# Second item
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>First item</li>
  <li>Second item</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Hint on a nested list {#lists-hint-nested}
[code om]
# Outer
##(a) Inner one
## Inner two
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Outer
    <ol type="a">
      <li>Inner one</li>
      <li>Inner two</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Hint without a following space is not a list {#lists-hint-no-space}
[code om]
#(A)First
[/code]
[code html]
<p>#(A)First</p>
[/code]

h2. Termination

h3. Blank line separates two bulleted lists {#lists-blank-line-bullets}
[code om]
* a

* b
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>a</li>
</ul>
<ul>
  <li>b</li>
</ul>
[/code]

h3. Blank line restarts hash numbering {#lists-blank-line-hash}
[code om]
# a

# b
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>a</li>
</ol>
<ol>
  <li>b</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Blank line separates explicitly numbered lists {#lists-blank-line-explicit}
[code om]
1. a

2. b
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>a</li>
</ol>
<ol start="2">
  <li>b</li>
</ol>
[/code]

h3. Paragraph after a blank line {#lists-then-paragraph}
[code om]
* Item

Text after the list.
[/code]
[code html]
<ul>
  <li>Item</li>
</ul>
<p>Text after the list.</p>
[/code]

h2. Profiles

h3. Lists are not allowed in the inline profile {#lists-profile-inline}
; profile
: inline
[code om]
* Item
[/code]
[code error]
feature-not-in-profile 1
[/code]

h3. Lists are allowed in the basic profile {#lists-profile-basic}
; profile
: basic
[code om]
# Item
[/code]
[code html]
<ol>
  <li>Item</li>
</ol>
[/code]
